WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.760
Avengers: Endgame​ left the stories of many
of our favorite heroes up in the air, but

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.940
perhaps none so much as Mark Ruffalo's Bruce
Banner.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.180
Fans of the Green Goliath would love to know:
is Banner going to play a part in the ​Disney+

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.140
She-Hulk​ limited series, or what?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.140
Well, we have no way of knowing for sure,
but the short answer is: it's pretty likely.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.440
Not only would it make narrative sense, but
it would give Marvel Studios the opportunity

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.940
to continue to capitalize on the Hulk without
needing to worry about his film rights.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.780
It's well-known that in the '90s, at a time
when Marvel Comics was in serious financial

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.850
jeopardy, the publisher sold the film rights
to many of its most beloved characters: Spider-Man

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.360
went to Sony Pictures, while the X-Men, the
Fantastic Four, and many of their associated

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.940
characters wound up at Fox Studios.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.039
Spider-Man had a five-film run during the
brief period of time that Marvel and Sony

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:54.129
were able to play ball, while the Fox-owned
properties are only now being prepped for

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:59.539
entry into the franchise following the acquisition
of Fox by Marvel's parent company, Disney.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:03.980
But many casual fans are unaware that the
MCU had been impacted from the very beginning

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:08.620
by a third deal: the one that Marvel made
with Universal for the Hulk's film rights.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.380
That's how the Ang Lee 2003 Hulk was made,
and the agreement is also the reason why 2008's

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.920
The Incredible Hulk was distributed by Universal.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:21.260
The studio had secured the film rights to
the Green Goliath in the early '00s, but only

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.860
for the 2003 film.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.260
Following that, the studio retained "right
of first refusal" to distribute, not produce,

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.620
any solo Hulk picture.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.180
Universal retains the right to distribute
any future Hulk movies, from now until the

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.640
end of time, and as far as Disney is concerned,
this simply won't do.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.520
Nothing in that deal, though, says that Marvel
can't use the Hulk as a supporting character

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.930
— which is why Bruce Banner has been featured
in team-up films since the Disney acquisition.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:52.380
So, considering this history, it seems likely
that Marvel Studios can use Banner as a supporting

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.960
character in She-Hulk if they want to do so.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.550
It's unclear whether Universal's deal with
Marvel covered the character's television

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:03.530
rights at all, but, considering that Universal
hasn't even attempted to make a Hulk TV project

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.780
in the last couple of decades, we're thinking
that it did not.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.550
Of course, it's likely that Banner is involved
on some level, since She-Hulk's entire origin

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:12.840
revolves around her cousin.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:17.300
In the comics, Walters' superpowers comes
from a blood transfusion given to her by her

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:22.240
cousin after the young, crusading attorney
was shot and grievously wounded by gangsters.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.340
Obviously, this scenario will probably be
updated in some way, but it would be pretty

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.000
hard to come up with an origin for She-Hulk
which excludes the original Jade Giant.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.940
Including Banner in the events of She-Hulk
would also help to tie up several narrative

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.520
loose ends, including those left dangling
by The Incredible Hulk.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.240
Is Emil Blonsky, AKA the Abomination, still
sitting in the Raft plotting his revenge?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.780
Did Samuel Stearns become the Leader, or did
that weird mutation going on with his head

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.060
just kind of peter out?

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.420
We also submit that, although Banner's arc
was indeed wrapped up pretty satisfactorily

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.380
by the events of Endgame, he didn't exactly
get an tear-jerking, iconic sendoff like Stark

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.200
and Rogers did.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:04.340
It'd be nice if he could be given a proper
goodbye, while at the same time passing the

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.600
torch to a new Hulk.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.920
At any rate, we'll all just have to stay tuned
for an official announcement, but we're pretty

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.600
sure that Ruffalo's Bruce Banner will figure
prominently in the She-Hulk Disney+ series.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.520
We'll be keeping an eye out for any news to
come, and we'll keep you up to speed.

